   "title": "Start here",
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Krea 2 - Eight views of a person\n\n1. **Load Reference** (stage 1): a clear photo of the person (the sample opens). Head and shoulders or upper body works best.\n2. **Run** once. Eight views of the same person - close-up, front, both three-quarters, both profiles, back, full body - are saved to `ComfyUI/output/krea2_views/`, plus one contact sheet.\n\nEdit the views in **Prompt List**: one per line.\n\n**GPU:** 24 GB minimum (RTX 4090, A5000, L4), 32 GB comfortable (RTX 5090). The reference portrait adds a little memory on top of plain text-to-image.\n\n**Out of memory, or very slow?** Use a smaller image size (832 x 832), or on an RTX 50xx the nvfp4 model (`KREA2_MODELS=nvfp4,raw` at deploy). ComfyUI moves models off the GPU when it has to: slower, but it still finishes.\n\n**Red nodes are the ones you set.** Stages run left to right with a note under each.\n\nFull instructions: https://github.com/tenitsky/krea2-image"
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
